#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:2
msgid "Instances"
msgstr "Instancias"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:7
msgid ""
"Instances are a great starting point for taking advantage of self service"
" features and spinning up both VMs and containers. In |morpheus| it may "
"be advisable to cover the definition of a few terms used within the "
"application so as to reduce confusion. These concepts are also covered in"
" greater detail in the `Provisioning Concepts "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/provisioning/concepts/concepts.html>`_"
" section."
msgstr ""
"Instancias son un great starting point para taking advantage de self "
"service features y spinning up both VMs y containers. En |morpheus| it "
"puede be advisable a cover el/la definition de un few terms used within "
"el/la aplicación so as a reduce confusion. Estos concepts son also covered "
"en greater detalle en el/la `Provisioning Concepts "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/provisioning/concepts/concepts.html>`_ "
"sección."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:9
msgid "Instance"
msgstr "Instancia"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:10
msgid ""
"A set of containers or virtual machines that can correlate to a single "
"horizontally-scalable entity or a service suite, like a database. It is "
"important to note that an Instance can contain one or more containers/VMs"
" depending on the Instance type and configuration."
msgstr ""
"Un establecer de containers o virtual machines que puede correlate a un "
"single horizontally-scalable entity o un service suite, like un database. "
"It es important a tenga en cuenta que un Instancia puede contener one o más "
"containers/VMs depending en el/la Instancia tipo y configuración."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:11
msgid "Container"
msgstr "Container"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:12
msgid "Typically a docker container provisioned via a |morpheus| Docker host."
msgstr "Typically un docker container provisioned via un |morpheus| Docker host."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:14
msgid "Virtual Machine"
msgstr "Virtual Machine"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:14
msgid "A virtualized compute server provisioned onto various hypervisor hosts."
msgstr "Un virtualized compute servidor provisioned onto various hypervisor hosts."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:16
msgid ""
"The top of the main Instances page shows overall statistics for the "
"listed Instances, including count, status, and resource utilization. You "
"can search for Instances by name, or filter by group, instance type, or "
"category."
msgstr ""
"El/La top de el/la main Instancias página shows overall statistics para "
"el/la listed Instancias, including count, estado, y recursos utilization. "
"You puede search para Instancias por nombre, o filter por group, instancia "
"tipo, o category."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:18
msgid ""
"Instances listed are determined by group access and role permissions. "
"When filtered to show Instances of \"All Statuses\", any Instances which "
"are in a state of pending removal due to a delayed delete policy in place"
" are not shown under this filter. Instead you must filter for \"Pending "
"Removal\" to see these Instances and prevent deletion, if desired."
msgstr ""
"Instancias listed son determined por group acceso y role permisos. Cuando "
"filtered a mostrar Instancias de \"Todos Statuses\", cualquier Instancias "
"cual son en un state de pending removal due a un delayed eliminar policy en "
"place son no shown bajo este filter. Instead you must filter para \"Pending "
"Removal\" a ver estos Instancias y prevent deletion, si desired."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/instances.rst:20
msgid ""
"The Instance list contains important information about each instance, "
"including the instance name, environment tag, instance type icon, IP "
"address and port info, Instance version, the number of virtual machines "
"or containers in the instance, the group the instance is in, and the "
"cloud or clouds the instance is in."
msgstr ""
"El/La Instancia lista contiene important información acerca de cada "
"instancia, including el/la instancia nombre, entorno tag, instancia tipo "
"icon, IP address y port info, Instancia versión, el/la number de virtual "
"machines o containers en el/la instancia, el/la group el/la instancia es "
"en, y el/la cloud o clouds el/la instancia es en."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:2
msgid "Creating Instances"
msgstr "Crear instancias"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:4
msgid ""
"The Instance catalog is the one-stop shop for selecting items to be "
"provisioned and pieced together. It contains not only basic container and"
" VM options but also tailored services for SQL databases, NoSQL "
"databases, cache stores, message busses, web servers, and even full-"
"fledged apps. The list contains a lot of items to choose from and they "
"are represented to the user based on what provisioning engines are "
"enabled and integrated in the |morpheus| environment."
msgstr ""
"El/La Instancia catálogo es el/la one-stop shop para selecting elementos a "
"be provisioned y pieced together. It contiene no solo basic container y VM "
"opciones pero also tailored services para SQL databases, NoSQL databases, "
"cache stores, message busses, web servidores, y even full-fledged apps. "
"El/La lista contiene un lot de elementos a choose desde y they son "
"represented a el/la usuario based en qué aprovisionamiento engines son "
"habilitado y integrated en el/la |morpheus| entorno."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:6
msgid ""
"To get started, simply click the :guilabel:`+ Add` button in the upper "
"right of the |ProIns| section. A modal will display allowing the catalog "
"to be searched. Once an item is selected it is just a matter of following"
" the steps through the wizard."
msgstr ""
"A obtener started, simply haga clic en el :guilabel:`+ Add` botón en el/la "
"upper right de el/la |ProIns| sección. Un modal será display allowing el/la "
"catálogo a be searched. Once un elemento es seleccionado it es just un "
"matter de siguiente el/la steps a través de el/la wizard."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:8
msgid ""
"The Instance catalog can be customized via role-based access control "
"(RBAC) thereby restricting access to non-sanctioned catalog items, as "
"well as added to via the |Lib| section. It is completely customizable."
msgstr ""
"The Instancia catálogo puede ser customized via role-based access control "
"(RBAC) thereby restricting access to non-sanctioned catálogo items, así "
"como added to via the |Lib| section. It is completely customizable."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:10
msgid ""
"The next step will ask for a Group and Cloud to be selected. The Group is"
" an abstract representation that can contain multiple cloud integrations."
" Clouds can be in multiple Groups and Groups are also useful for using "
"RBAC to restrict provisioning access and set retainment policies. If the "
"environment is new and these do not yet exist, it may be advisable to "
"refer to one of our starter guides, such as the guide on getting started "
"with |morpheus| and `VMware "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.html>`_."
" The wizard continues by allowing us to choose a name for the Instance as"
" well as an environment."
msgstr ""
"El/La siguiente step será ask para un Group y Cloud a be seleccionado. "
"El/La Group es un abstract representation que puede contener multiple cloud "
"integraciones. Clouds puede ser en multiple Groups y Groups son also useful "
"para using RBAC a restrict aprovisionamiento acceso y establecer retainment "
"policies. Si el/la entorno es nuevo y estos hacer no yet exist, it puede be "
"advisable a refer a one de our starter guides, como el/la guide en getting "
"started con |morpheus| y `VMware "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/getting_started/guides/vmware_guide.html>`_. "
"El/La wizard continues por allowing us a choose un nombre para el/la "
"Instancia así como un entorno."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:12
msgid ""
"Currently the Environment option is mostly useful for presenting the user"
" with informative metadata around the Instance when coming back to it "
"later."
msgstr ""
"Currently el/la Environment opción es mostly useful para presenting el/la "
"usuario con informative metadata around el/la Instancia cuando coming back "
"a it later."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:14
msgid ""
"Moving on, it is now time to configure the Instance. Depending on the "
"Instance Configuration that is chosen, fields will change. This can "
"include cloud-specific fields (i.e. Datastore for VMware or Network). "
"There will also be options like setting an initial user account. Some of "
"these fields are optional and will be represented as such."
msgstr ""
"Moving en, it es now time a configurar el/la Instancia. Depending en el/la "
"Instancia Configuration que es chosen, campos será change. Este puede "
"incluir cloud-specific campos (i.e. Datastore para VMware o Network). There "
"será also be opciones like setting un initial usuario account. Some de "
"estos campos son opcional y será represented as such."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:16
msgid ""
"Configuration options provided in this screen are very powerful. An "
"example is MySQL where a Master/Slave or Master/Master layout can be "
"selected. These configurations will automatically deploy two MySQL VMs or"
" containers and link them together to provide replication. These types of"
" configurations exist for a wide range of Instance types and are "
"optimized for high performance and scale. It is even possible to "
"provision entire sharded MongoDB clusters."
msgstr ""
"Configuration opciones provided en este screen son very powerful. Un "
"ejemplo es MySQL donde un Master/Slave o Master/Master layout puede ser "
"seleccionado. Estos configuraciones será automáticamente deploy two MySQL "
"VMs o containers y link them together a proporcionar replication. Estos "
"tipos de configuraciones exist para un wide range de Instancia tipos y son "
"optimized para high performance y scale. It es even possible a provision "
"entire sharded MongoDB clústeres."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:18
msgid ""
"One last step before the Instance can be provisioned is the Automation "
"step. This wizard step may or may not appear depending on the "
"capabilities of the Instance type or previous configurations in the "
"account. It is here one can easily select a post-provisioning workflow to"
" run (see more on Tasks and Workflows elsewhere in |morpheus| "
"documentation), assign a load balancer, or even configure the backup job "
"that gets created."
msgstr ""
"One last step antes de el/la Instancia puede ser provisioned es el/la "
"Automation step. Este wizard step puede o puede no appear depending en "
"el/la capabilities de el/la Instancia tipo o previous configuraciones en "
"el/la account. It es here one puede easily seleccionar un "
"post-aprovisionamiento flujo de trabajo a ejecutar (ver más en Tareas y "
"Flujos de trabajo elsewhere en |morpheus| documentación), assign un cargar "
"balancer, o even configurar el/la backup job que gets creado."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:20
msgid ""
"Now that the steps are completed for provisioning the selected Instance "
"type, simply review your selections and complete. The Instance will "
"automatically show up in the Instances list and its provisioning state "
"will be represented. Depending on what was provisioned this step can "
"range from seconds to minutes (typically a container configuration will "
"be rather quick if the Instance type has previously been provisioned "
"before)."
msgstr ""
"Now que el/la steps son completed para aprovisionamiento el/la seleccionado "
"Instancia tipo, simply review your selections y complete. El/La Instancia "
"será automáticamente mostrar up en el/la Instancias lista y its "
"aprovisionamiento state será represented. Depending en qué fue provisioned "
"este step puede range desde seconds a minutes (typically un container "
"configuración será rather quick si el/la Instancia tipo tiene previamente "
"been provisioned antes de)."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:23
msgid "Converting Discovered Resources to Managed Instances"
msgstr "Converting Discovered Resources to Managed Instancias"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:25
msgid ""
"When creating new cloud integrations (or updating existing ones), users "
"may opt for |morpheus| to onboard any existing resources that currently "
"reside in the Cloud. For example, these may be virtual machines that "
"exist on vCenter hosts prior to integration with |morpheus|, EC2 "
"instances pre-existing on an Amazon AWS account, or virtual machines that"
" are running on a KVM host. With the Add/Edit Cloud modal open, mark "
"INVENTORY EXISTING INSTANCES for |morpheus| to automatically onboard "
"these resources. Not only will |morpheus| inventory these instances at "
"the time the cloud is integrated (or updated), it will also continue to "
"poll the target cloud every five minutes (by default) for newly added or "
"removed servers. Users can see these discovered servers by looking in "
"|InfCom|. Depending on the type of resource, it may appear on the Virtual"
" Machines tab, the Containers tab, or another tab. Additionally, we can "
"see a list of discovered servers on Cloud detail pages (|InfClo| > "
"Selected Cloud). Just click on the tabs for VMs, Containers or Hosts tab."
" Discovered resources will be indicated as such whereas containers which "
"are associated with a managed Instance will be marked as a \"Managed\"."
msgstr ""
"Cuando creating nuevo cloud integraciones (o updating existente ones), "
"usuarios puede opt para |morpheus| a onboard cualquier existente recursos "
"que actualmente reside en el/la Cloud. Por ejemplo, estos puede be virtual "
"machines que exist en vCenter hosts prior a integraciones con |morpheus|, "
"EC2 instancias pre-existente en un Amazon AWS account, o virtual machines "
"que son running en un KVM host. Con el/la Agregar/Editar Cloud modal abrir, "
"mark INVENTORY EXISTING INSTANCES para |morpheus| a automáticamente onboard "
"estos recursos. No solo será |morpheus| inventory estos instancias en el/la "
"time el/la cloud es integrated (o actualizado), it será also continue a "
"poll el/la target cloud every five minutes (de forma predeterminada) para "
"newly added o removed servidores. Usuarios puede ver estos discovered "
"servidores por looking en |InfCom|. Depending en el/la tipo de recursos, it "
"puede appear en el/la Virtual Machines pestaña, el/la Containers pestaña, o "
"another pestaña. Adicionalmente, we puede ver un lista de discovered "
"servidores en Cloud detalle páginas (|InfClo| > Selected Cloud). Just haga "
"clic en el/la pestañas para VMs, Containers o Hosts pestaña. Discovered "
"recursos será indicated as such whereas containers cual son associated con "
"un managed Instancia será marked as un \"Managed\"."

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:27
msgid ""
"Additionally, |morpheus| allows users to convert discovered resources "
"into managed Instances. Begin from the server detail page (|InfComVir| > "
"selected machine) and from the ACTIONS menu select \"Convert to "
"Managed\". At this point, we must make a number of selections:"
msgstr ""
"Adicionalmente, |morpheus| permite un los usuarios convert discovered "
"recursos en managed Instancias. Begin desde el/la servidor detalle página "
"(|InfComVir| > seleccionado machine) y desde el/la ACTIONS menu seleccionar "
"\"Convert a Managed\". En este point, we must make un number de selections:"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:29
msgid "Assign to the primary Tenant or one of the Subtenants"
msgstr "Assign to the primary Inquilino or one of the Subtenants"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:30
msgid ""
"Select a Group (this dropdown contains a filtered list of Groups which "
"the associated Cloud is in)"
msgstr ""
"Seleccionar un Group (este dropdown contiene un filtered lista de Groups "
"cual el/la associated Cloud es en)"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:31
msgid "Username and password for a seeded account"
msgstr "Username y password para un seeded account"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:32
msgid ""
"Opt to install |morpheus| Agent or not (for more on |morpheus| Agent, "
"click `here "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/getting_started/functionality/agent/morpheus_agent.html>`_)"
msgstr ""
"Opt to install |morpheus| Agent or not (para más on |morpheus| Agent, click "
"`here "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/getting_started/functionality/agent/morpheus_agent.html>`_)"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:33
msgid ""
"Select the Instance Type which should be associated with the new Instance"
" containing this VM"
msgstr ""
"Seleccione el Instancia Type which debería ser associated with the new "
"Instancia containing this VM"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:34
msgid ""
"Select a version number for the Instance (such as 20.04 for a basic "
"Ubuntu Instance)"
msgstr ""
"Select a version number for the Instancia (como 20.04 for a basic Ubuntu "
"Instancia)"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:35
msgid "Select a Layout, Instance Types often have multiple Layout configurations"
msgstr "Select a Layout, Instancia Types often have multiple Layout configuraciones"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:36
msgid "Identify the operating system"
msgstr "Identify el/la operating system"

#: ../../provisioning/instances/creating_instances.rst:37
msgid ""
"Select a Plan (this dropdown contains a filtered list of plans which "
"correlate to the size of the VM)"
msgstr ""
"Seleccionar un Plan (este dropdown contiene un filtered lista de plans cual "
